menu "Cyber Fly brain downlink"

config FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    bool "Receive real MPRC brain frames from the cloud"
    default y
    help
        Off = the board animates from the built-in fake generator only
        (useful when there is no cloud reachable). On = the board keeps a UDP
        socket open, emits a 68 B MPRB feature frame every 50 ms, and feeds
        every MPRC reply into fly_state_decode().

        The board is behind a phone-hotspot NAT, so the cloud never connects
        to us: stage1_loop.js answers each MPRB with an MPRC sent straight back
        to the sender's observed address:port. Our own 20 Hz upstream traffic is
        what keeps the NAT mapping open.

config FLY_LINK_HOST
    string "Cloud orchestrator IPv4 (dotted quad)"
    default "192.168.1.100"
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    help
        The default is a placeholder on purpose: point it at your own cloud
        orchestrator with `idf.py menuconfig` (or edit sdkconfig). A literal
        address, not a hostname, on purpose: lwIP DNS would add a blocking
        resolver call to the link task's first send.

config FLY_LINK_PORT
    int "Cloud orchestrator UDP port"
    range 1 65535
    default 33333
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE

config FLY_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID (phone hotspot, 2.4 GHz)"
    default "your-ssid"
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    help
        The default is a placeholder on purpose: set your own hotspot name with
        `idf.py menuconfig` (or edit sdkconfig). The ESP32-S31 radio is 2.4 GHz
        only, so the hotspot must be on a 2.4 GHz band (on iOS that is the
        "maximum compatibility" switch). The board retries forever, so switching
        the hotspot on after boot is fine.

config FLY_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default "your-wifi-password"
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    help
        The default is a placeholder on purpose: set your own 2.4 GHz hotspot
        credentials with `idf.py menuconfig` (or edit sdkconfig). An EMPTY
        password silently fails on any WPA2 access point: the driver retries
        forever with no credentials, and the symptom is indistinguishable from
        the hotspot being off. Leave this empty only for a genuinely open
        network.

config FLY_WIFI_TIMEOUT_SEC
    int "Per-attempt association timeout (seconds)"
    range 5 120
    default 20
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE

config FLY_WIFI_RETRY_SEC
    int "Seconds between association attempts"
    range 1 300
    default 10
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    help
        How long to wait before retrying after a failed attempt. Lower this while
        commissioning a hotspot (5 s feels responsive); raise it for a permanent
        install so a hotspot that is off for hours does not keep the radio busy.

config FLY_MIC_GAIN_DB
    int "Microphone input gain (dB)"
    range 0 50
    default 30
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    help
        Task A measured a -44.7 dBFS noise floor at 30 dB gain in a quiet room
        and a clean band ordering (-60.4 / -71.6 / -73.0 dBFS) at that setting.
        The cloud's dose-response split sits between about -48 and -36 dBFS, so
        30 dB places the room floor and music on opposite sides of it.

        >>> FIRST-HARDWARE-RUN WARNING (2026-10-06): at 30 dB the room floor
        >>> already reached -31.8 dBFS, and the orchestrator's
        >>> level01 = (rms - GATE_DB)/GATE_SPAN saturates at 1.00 once rms
        >>> reaches -28 dBFS. The result was a fly that escaped continuously in
        >>> silence (aud 1.00, esc 80+ on the board with nothing playing).
        >>> Read the new "上行电平 rms=... dBFS" line in the log, then either
        >>> lower this gain or raise the cloud's GATE_DB / GATE_SPAN so the
        >>> quiet room lands near 0.1 and music lands near 1.0.

config FLY_IMU_ENABLE
    bool "Read the BMI270 for steering (accel[0])"
    default y
    depends on FLY_LINK_ENABLE
    help
        The v4 subcircuit's LEFT/RIGHT (DNa) neurons have no named sensory
        input, so the board must supply the signed sideways acceleration
        directly - a cloud round trip is ~100 ms, far too slow for a balance
        reflex (design doc 0.5).

        Off = accel[0] stays 0 and the fly never steers, which is the right
        choice when the board is mounted in a fixed enclosure.

endmenu
